/.lake
/conformance/.lake
/.direnv

# `lake update` run inside conformance/ writes a lean-toolchain there. The root
# file is meant to be this repository's only one: a second copy is what Lake
# picks when building from that directory, so one left at a stale version
# builds everything on it and still reports a pass. Ignore rather than delete,
# because deleting it does not stop the next `lake update` re-creating it.
/conformance/lean-toolchain
